C o m p i l a t i o n


      Maddie Witte
      maddie.witte@usu.edu
      October 2, 2026
      CEE 6410 ENGR Systems Analysis
       
      HW 2 PROBLEM:
      A field will be planted with hay and grain and watered using excess from an aqueduct.
       
                           Monthly water demand (ac-ft)
                           June             July           August           Return ($/acre)
      Hay                  2                1              1                100
      Grain                1                2              0                120
       
      Determine the optimal water allocation plan.
       
       
      THE SOLUTION:
      Uses General Algebraic Modeling System to Solve this Linear Program. Below:
       
  22   
  23  * 1. DEFINE the SETS
  24  SETS crop crops growing /Hay, Grain/
  25       month resources /June, July, August/;
  26   
  27  * 2. DEFINE input data
  28  PARAMETERS
  29     c(crop) Objective function coefficients ($ per plant)
  30           /Hay 100,
  31           Grain 120/
  32     b(month) Right hand constraint values (per resource)
  33            /June 14000,
  34             July  18000,
  35             August 6000 /
  36     MaxArea the maximum area the crops can cover (acres)
  37           /1000/;
  38   
  39  TABLE A(crop,month) Left hand side constraint coefficients
  40                   June   July  August
  41   Hay             2      1     1
  42   Grain           1      2     0;
  43   
  44  * 3. DEFINE the variables
  45  VARIABLES X(crop) plants planted (acres)
  46            VPROFIT  total profit ($)
  47            Y(month)  value of water used (ac-ft)
  48            VREDCOST total reduced cost ($)
  49            Z max area constraint (acres);
  50   
  51  * Non-negativity constraints
  52  POSITIVE VARIABLES X, Y, Z;
  53   
  54  * 4. COMBINE variables and data in equations
  55  EQUATIONS
  56     PROFIT_PRIMAL Total profit ($) and objective function value
  57     RES_CONS_PRIMAL(month) Resource constraints
  58     REDCOST_DUAL Reduced Cost ($) associated with using resources
  59     RES_CONS_DUAL(crop) Profit levels
  60     CROP_AREA max area of the crops;
  61   
  62  *Primal Equations
  63  PROFIT_PRIMAL..                 VPROFIT =E= SUM(crop,c(crop)*X(crop));
  64  RES_CONS_PRIMAL(month) ..    SUM(crop,A(crop,month)*X(crop)) =L= b(month);
  65  CROP_AREA..                   SUM(crop,X(crop)) =L= MaxArea;
  66   
  67  *Dual Equations
  68  REDCOST_DUAL..                 VREDCOST =E= SUM(month,b(month)*Y(month))+MaxArea*Z;
  69  RES_CONS_DUAL(crop)..          sum(month,A(crop,month)*Y(month)) +Z =G= c(crop);
  70   
  71   
  72  * 5. DEFINE the MODELS
  73  *PRIMAL model
  74  MODEL CROP_PRIMAL /PROFIT_PRIMAL, RES_CONS_PRIMAL, CROP_AREA/;
  75  *Set the options file to print out range of basis information
  76  CROP_PRIMAL.optfile = 1;
  77   
  78  *DUAL model
  79  MODEL CROP_DUAL /REDCOST_DUAL, RES_CONS_DUAL/;
  80   
  81  * 6. SOLVE the MODELS
  82  * Solve the PLANTING PRIMAL model using a Linear Programming Solver (see File=>Options=>Solvers)
  83  *     to maximize VPROFIT
  84  SOLVE CROP_PRIMAL USING LP MAXIMIZING VPROFIT;
  85   
  86  * Solve the PLANTING DUAL model using a Linear Programming Solver (see File=>Options=>Solvers)
  87  *     to maximize VPROFIT
  88  SOLVE CROP_DUAL USING LP MINIMIZING VREDCOST;
  89  *Order does not matter!
  90   
  91  * 6. CLick File menu => RUN (F9) or Solve icon and examine solution report in .LST file
  92   
  93  * 7 . Dump all data and results to GAMS proprietary file storage .gdx and to Excel
  94  Execute_Unload "Ex2-1Dual.gdx";
  95  * Dump the gdx file to an Excel workbook
  96  Execute "gdx2xls Ex2-1Dual.gdx"
  97  * To open the GDX file in the GAMS IDE, select File => Open.
  98  * In the Open window, set Filetype to .gdx and select the file.


